[322.826221, "o", "        \"answer\": \"Paxlovid (nirmatrelvir co-packaged with ritonavir) is a strong inhibitor of CYP3A, and an inhibitor of CYP2D6, P-gp and OATP1B1. Co-administration of Paxlovid with drugs primarily metabolized by CYP3A and CYP2D6 or transported by P-gp or OATP1B1 may result in increased plasma concentrations of such drugs, increasing the risk of severe, life-threatening, or fatal events. Additionally, nirmatrelvir and ritonavir are CYP3A substrates; therefore, concomitant use of strong CYP3A inducers may decrease Paxlovid plasma concentrations and reduce its therapeutic effect.\",\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         \"citations\": [\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rse of the oral solution should be administered using the calibrated cup (sup\u001b[?2004h> "]
[322.826248, "o", "            {\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
